# Build Buyer Marketplace Module

Design and develop a modern, responsive, production-ready Marketplace page for the AgriChain platform. This will allow buyers to discover fresh farm products directly from verified farmers. The implementation spans the Rust (Axum) backend, MongoDB, and React (Vite) frontend with Tailwind CSS.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Cart & Purchasing Flow:** This implementation will build the full UI for the Marketplace (including 'Add to Cart' and 'Buy Now' buttons) and integrate product fetching and filtering from the backend. The backend APIs for actually creating a Cart, processing Orders, and handling Payments are assumed to be outside the scope of this specific page build and will be mocked or added in a subsequent phase if needed.
> **Categories:** "Popular Crops" categories (Tomato, Potato, Onion, etc.) will be hardcoded in the frontend as quick-filters, as is common practice for visually rich categories unless a dynamic category API is preferred.

## Open Questions
- Do you want to use the browser's Geolocation API on the frontend to get the Buyer's current latitude/longitude to send to the `/farmers/nearby` endpoint, or should we use the Buyer's registered address from their profile?
- Should the `Add to Cart` and `Buy Now` buttons trigger any mock notifications, or should they be disabled pending the actual order management backend?

